                "letterSpacing": "0",
                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "A hold that clears (Track Hold = Clear track, or a Custom pedal whose Hold is Clear or Clear all) fills the held pedal's LED pill: red grows from both ends toward the centre over the long-press time (800 ms by default). When it fires the ends meet and the pill shows full for a moment, then the empty-track state. Releasing early, a mode change, a lost link, or a hold that can no longer fire (a take locked) ends the fill at once and the pill shows its normal state. With two clear holds pending the newest fills, and the older one fills again if the newer settles first. The app streams the progress every 20 ms in the optional CLEAR_HOLD message (console firmware 2.6, protocol still 12, so older firmware shows no fill and nothing wrong). No screen mirrors the LED pill: Tracks draws no pedals, and the Custom face's Pending Hold bar already times the same hold."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "24",
